# A veteran-scheme sideshift, run up to avoid the wall that made the original
# capture's displacement figure unusable. See `sideshift-double-tap.inputs` for
# the gesture itself (timer confirmation, tap timing, why `l` is the button and
# not the axis) - this file exists only to fix the run-up, not to repeat that.
#
# `sideshift-double-tap.inputs`'s `180 cross` run-up grazes a wall on Talon's
# Junction around tick 60-90 (`input-bindings.md`'s runtime section), so the
# capture and its control were already 1.17 units apart by the time the first
# tap fired - a wall-contact residue much larger than the sideshift's own
# signal, and the "11.7 units of leftward displacement" figure was never a
# runtime measurement of the original to begin with (it came from `oag-trace
# drive` through our own simulation, which does not hit this wall on the same
# script). See `handover/sideshift-has-no-runtime-leg.md`.
#
# `Ship_UpdateAirbrakes` (`0x0884c9a4`) applies the sideshift as a constant
# world-space force (`craft.right * handling.sideshift`, divided by mass by the
# integrator like any other force - see `engine.md`'s "the sideshift is a
# force" section), not a velocity-scaled one. So a shorter run-up does not bias
# the measurement the way it would if the shift scaled with speed - the fix
# here is purely about clearing the wall, not about preserving a particular
# forward speed.
#
# `130 cross` was chosen off `data/traces/talons-junction-standing-start.csv`
# (the same launch profile - a stationary craft under `--hold cross`, no
# steering): that capture shows a clean, undisturbed speed climb through tick
# 130 (~90 units/s, well clear of both the 60-90 graze this script's own
# citation reports and the ~187 first-contact tick that capture itself shows -
# see the thread file for why those two disagree, which this file does not
# depend on either way). 130 ticks clears the disputed window with margin in
# both directions without needing to fall back to a token run-up.

# Reach speed on the opening straight, short enough to clear the wall.
130 cross

# Tap one: opens the left window.
1 cross l
3 cross

# Tap two: fires the sideshift.
1 cross l

# The shift itself is 0.2 s, and then a second of lockout. Hold the line
# through both so the displacement is measurable after it has settled.
100 cross
